---
layout: layout.webc
title: Import from Strava - The Distance
---

<div class="g-max-centered">
  <div class="contents">
    <header>
      <h2>Import from Strava</h2>
      <p>Bulk export and import your Strava data.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="import-body">
      <div class="import-intro">
        <p>
          <b
            >Due to Strava API Agreement restrictions, we can’t connect to your
            Strava account and import your data.</b
          >
          What you can do is export all of your Strava data and upload it here.
        </p>
        <p>
          The steps are listed below, if you run into trouble, see Strava’s
          documentation page “<a
            href="https://support.strava.com/hc/en-us/articles/216918437-Exporting-your-Data-and-Bulk-Export"
            >Exporting your Data and Bulk Export</a
          >”. Look for the “Bulk Export” section near the bottom.
        </p>

        <details>
          <summary><strong>Strava export steps</strong></summary>

          <ol>
            <li>
              Log into your <a href="https://strava.com">Strava account</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              Hover over your name in the upper right-hand corner of the Strava
              page
            </li>
            <li>
              Choose “Settings,” then find the “My Account” tab from the menu
              listed on the Left
            </li>
            <li>
              Select “Get Started” under “Download or Delete Your Account”
            </li>
            <li>Select “Request your archive” on the next page</li>
            <li>
              You will receive an email with a link to download your data (this
              may take a few hours)
            </li>
            <li>Once you have the zip file, upload it here</li>
          </ol>
        </details>
      </div>
      <div class="import-workspace">
        <import-wizard></import-wizard>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

